{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "170", "x": 0.8961566778142049, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.03758657078943087, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "started to resemble programs today? Maya: Yes. And unlike programs from the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.12334338960510077, "w": 0.825968325120572, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "18th century, they always used color and there was a greater variety of designs.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.1436641300790535, "w": 0.8260117957009852, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "But personally, I think 18th century programs were superior because they told the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.16398487055300617, "w": 0.8262754898821711, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "theatergoers so many things, including about the actors.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.18445393154231154, "w": 0.5834766119562755, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Finn: And about the writer, the plot, and sometimes the history of the play.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.21471252375881908, "w": 0.7635310383532524, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Maya: That's right. What should we say about theater programs in the 20th", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2449711914181116, "w": 0.8264438358563186, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "century?", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2652919318920643, "w": 0.10022387092600436, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Finn: I reckon the most important thing is the dramatic change they underwent", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2955876419588025, "w": 0.8260917651649529, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "during World War II.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3160567029481079, "w": 0.21234845402109534, "h": 0.018822616509687834, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Maya: When the government imposed restrictions on the use of paper.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3463152763039192, "w": 0.7232165861179367, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Finn: Yeah, but that was only in the UK. In the USA, programs, or rather playbills,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3765738685204267, "w": 0.8265346729653897, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "continued to be published in the same format, while here in the UK, programs", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.39689460899437934, "w": 0.8260120007508928, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "became merely a single sheet of paper folded to create four pages for text.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.41721534946833205, "w": 0.7742143435896222, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Maya: What I don't really get is that after the war, they didn't go back to being", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.44747397940623207, "w": 0.8266893831206812, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "more than one sheet or change in any way for over 25 years. I know there were", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.46796774790763207, "w": 0.8258813839597454, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "paper shortages after the war, but only for 5 or 10 years.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4882884883815848, "w": 0.581460868839519, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Finn: Hmm, strange.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5185471183194849, "w": 0.21557360712417198, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Maya: I've got some pictures of programs we could include on the slides for our", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5488057482573848, "w": 0.8268535255717228, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "presentation. Finn: I found a couple too, Maya. Let's go through and see what we", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5692748092466902, "w": 0.8259682225956181, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "think. Um, this is an old one for a play called Ruie Blass.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5895955497206429, "w": 0.5711806917215099, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Maya: Never heard of that, but the program looks very decorative. Good enough", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6198541419371504, "w": 0.826047064285094, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "to put in a frame on the wall. The images are just beautiful. Finn, what did you find?", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6401748824111031, "w": 0.8323007788923266, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Finn: I've got some pages from a program for Of Lancha. I thought this was a good", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6704705924778414, "w": 0.8262198188322551, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "program to show, not because of the pictures, but because it contains articles", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6909396534671467, "w": 0.826077001571605, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "written by members of the theater company, so we can learn how the production", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7112603939410994, "w": 0.8263518709727558, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "was created and the thoughts and feelings of the cast.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7317294549304048, "w": 0.563520949897798, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Maya: Good. I've got a copy of a program that's now in a museum. It's for the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7619880471469123, "w": 0.8259511009283327, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "tragedy of Jane Shaw, and it's said to be the earliest surviving document to have", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.782308787620865, "w": 0.8261427200669939, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "been printed on Australia's first printing press. Oh, fantastic.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8026295280948177, "w": 0.6230351477071884, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Finn: Another program to talk about is for the Sailors Festival. It comes from the", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8328881957541102, "w": 0.825883742033683, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "British Library's digitized collection of programs that was started a few years ago.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8533571813006305, "w": 0.8264039536492885, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "It already comprises over 200,000 programs, which is amazing.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8737026670080704, "w": 0.6476269881767198, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Maya: Huh. Wish I'd known about it while I was doing my research.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.903961334667363, "w": 0.675040776737252, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}], "source": "pdf text layer"}